<urn:atm:triage:finding/R7-QA1-RSH-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "R7-QA1-RSH-003" ;
  triage:title "There is no end-to-end deadline for one judge call. Each Haiku or Luna judge makes two busy-retry exchanges (count, then message), and each exchange gets its own 90 s start budget and up to 4 sends. Backends in a run are judged sequentially, each with its own budget. Worst-case wall time is about 210 s per exchange, about 420 s per backend, and more than 20 minutes for a three-backend run." ;
  triage:description "There is no end-to-end deadline for one judge call. Each Haiku or Luna judge makes two busy-retry exchanges (count, then message), and each exchange gets its own 90 s start budget and up to 4 sends. Backends in a run are judged sequentially, each with its own budget. Worst-case wall time is about 210 s per exchange, about 420 s per backend, and more than 20 minutes for a three-backend run." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-a-refine" ;
